    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i tried running it locally and it seems fine there... so it's definitely something in the pipeline. i've checked the runner specs and they look consistent. it's like something is just messing with the execution randomly. any specific ways to check for race conditions or maybe resource contention between different builds running at the same time?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To check for contention, coordinate your Jenkins jobs to run sequentially, one after the other, and see if the failures disappear. If not, investigate shared resources like network mounts, databases, or temporary file directories to ensure they aren't being corrupted or locked by parallel builds. You can also add artificial delays (`sleep` commands) strategically within the test stage of the pipeline to try and force a timing-related race condition to occur reliably.",
      "source": "target",
